  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/A819F0">Definition <span data-tag="A819F0">1.1.3.6</span>.</a>equivalence!of topological categories Let $F: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ be a functor between topological categories. We will say that $F$ is a <em>weak equivalence</em>, or simply an <em>equivalence</em>, if the induced functor $\rm {h} \it { \calC } \rightarrow \rm {h} \it { \calD }$ is an equivalence of $\calH $-enriched categories. </p>
